PocketRoll is a fork of an openFPGA Game Boy / Game Boy Color core for the
Analogue Pocket. It is distributed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 (see LICENSE). The GPL-licensed upstream files carry
"GPL-3.0-or-later" headers, and those headers stay as they are.

This file lists the work PocketRoll builds on and every licence other than
the GPL found in the source headers. Each file's own header is authoritative;
keep it intact when you copy or modify the file. Any distribution of this
core, including a release zip, must ship LICENSE and this NOTICE.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Upstream projects
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

openFPGA-GBC, by budude2
  https://github.com/budude2/openfpga-GBC
  The Analogue Pocket port this repository is forked from: everything under
  src/ and pkg/ comes from it, apart from the PocketRoll changes listed in
  README.md. The upstream README is kept as README.budude2.md. The upstream
  repository has no LICENSE file; its files carry the licences listed below.

Gameboy_MiSTer, by the MiSTer-devel contributors
  https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Gameboy_MiSTer
  The MiSTer Game Boy core that openFPGA-GBC is ported from (src/gb/).
  It descends from the MiST Game Boy core by Till Harbaum. Files in src/gb/
  that carry no header of their own (mappers, savestates, sound, HDMA, ...)
  come from this project and are distributed here under the GPL.

